[task-01] Keep each stage's answer format the same across a review run, so that a
    provider able to reuse a repeated request is offered one.
    -> keep-stage-answer-format-stable-within-run  [invariant/explicit]
       Each stage's answer format stays the same across a review run.
    -> offer-reusable-request-when-provider-can-reuse  [functional/explicit]
       A provider able to reuse a repeated request is offered one.

[constraint-01] Every call a stage makes within one run declares the same answer format,
    whatever items that particular call asks about.
    -> same-answer-format-within-run  [invariant/explicit]
       Every call a stage makes within one run declares the same answer format, whatever
       items that particular call asks about.

[constraint-02] An answer says which item it is about, naming that item by the
    identifier the request gave it.
    -> answer-identifies-item-by-request-id  [functional/explicit]
       An answer says which item it is about, naming that item by the identifier the
       request gave it.

[constraint-03] A call is answered about as many items as its answer format provides
    for, and a call asking about fewer items than that is still answered in full.
    -> answer-full-item-set-per-format  [functional/explicit]
       A call is answered about as many items as its answer format provides for, and a
       call asking about fewer items than that is still answered in full.

[constraint-04] An answer naming an item its call did not ask about is recorded as an
    answer not obtained, and is never read as a judgement about any item.
    -> unasked-item-answers-are-not-judgements  [functional/explicit]
       An answer naming an item its call did not ask about is recorded as an answer not
       obtained, and is never read as a judgement about any item.

[constraint-05] A conclusion that holds only if every item was judged is withheld for a
